-- gold-v8.sql  (task #386)  -  the morning check of the 1-hour MACD e-mails for GOLD (XAU/USD), rule v8.
-- ONE read-only statement (WITH ... SELECT) for mcp__Supabase__execute_sql. Replace the two markers START_MS and END_MS (each written once, in double curly braces, in the first CTE) by the epoch
-- milliseconds of the range: bars are judged by their OPEN time, START_MS <= open < END_MS; the Routine's day is (X-2d) 21:00 UTC .. (X-1d) 21:00 UTC,
-- END_MS = START_MS + 86400000. Nothing else is to be edited. Bars that opened before 2026-10-30 02:00 UTC (1793325600000) were judged by the v7 rule on the 15-minute chart (from 2026-10-26 10:15 / 10:00 UTC), v6, v4 or v3: see README.md v8.1 for the file of each day.
-- It recounts the rule macdx_12_26_9_w600_1h_z95of120_v8 (signal-alerts v33, #386, the v6 rule on the 1-hour chart again: the MACD line, the blue line, comes into the top / bottom 95% band of the MACD pane of the newest 120 bars)
-- from the closed bars of the ONE stored row public.live_chart_fallback (XAU/USD, 1h; Twelve Data), and compares the expected entries with public.signal_alerts
-- (pair XAU/USD, kind signal, interval 1h, that rule id).
-- The row is the LATEST read: production judged each bar on the row as it was about a minute after the close. No user_id / event_id / e-mail is read; nothing is written.
-- Result: the same columns as pairs-v6.sql: row_type (RUN | SUMMARY | LINE), instrument, bar_open_utc, side, verdict, data (json). See README.md.
